  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the man in the image",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the man (person) in the selfie, as the meme implies that the viewer (user) is identifying with or imagining themselves as the person depicted, who is then labeled as 'i am racist' and 'i vote for donald'. This projection is implicit, as the meme uses the man's image to represent the user's potential self-identification with the hateful political stance. The user is not explicitly addressed with deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but the framing of the image and text creates an implicit identification where the viewer is expected to see themselves in the role of the man, thereby internalizing the meme's hateful message.",
